--- !u!114 &949993653
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 949993652}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: c0eb0a6540eb14d528d5f4c74fd9593c, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: PlutonyX.Game::PlutonyX.Game.ExploreController
  Player: {fileID: 1287775343}
  Cam: {fileID: 546289486}
  Spots:
  - Title: Habitat
    Text: Home for four people. A sol, one day on Mars, is about 24.6 hours long, and nights can fall to about -153 degrees Celsius. (NASA Mars facts)
    Center: {x: 0.5, y: 0.030227661, z: 0}
    Radius: 5.4
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: -5, y: 0.26016235, z: 0}
    Radius: 3.9
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: -9.5, y: 0.4437561, z: 0.3}
    Radius: 4
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: -13.5, y: 0.6016998, z: 0.3}
    Radius: 4
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: 5.2, y: -0.13114929, z: 2.9}
    Radius: 3.6
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: 9.2, y: -0.280365, z: 4.4}
    Radius: 3.6
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: 12.4, y: -0.40174866, z: 5.5}
    Radius: 3.2
  - Title: Greenhouse
    Text: Astronauts really grow lettuce, kale and mizuna on the International Space Station under pink LED lights. Fresh food keeps its vitamins. (NASA Veggie)
    Center: {x: -18, y: 1.0661926, z: 12}
    Radius: 4.2
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: -20.6, y: 1.2647247, z: 16.5}
    Radius: 3.4
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: -15.4, y: 0.8506012, z: 7.5}
    Radius: 3.4
  - Title: Air Maker
    Text: NASA's MOXIE experiment on the Perseverance rover made 122 grams of oxygen out of Mars air, up to 12 grams an hour. Each person needs about 0.84 kg a day. (NASA)
    Center: {x: 13, y: -0.32014465, z: 14.5}
    Radius: 3.6
  - Title: 
    Text: 
    Center: {x: 17.2, y: -0.5063629, z: 16.2}
    Radius: 2.6
  - Title: Solar field
    Text: Mars is about 1.5 times farther from the Sun than Earth, so panels get less than half the sunlight. Dust makes it worse. (NASA Mars facts)
    Center: {x: 37.6, y: -1.276413, z: -36.2}
    Radius: 0
  - Title: Storm shelter
    Text: On 20 May 2024 the Curiosity rover measured its biggest radiation surge in 12 years. NASA says cliffs or lava tubes would give astronauts extra shielding. The Storm Shield here is future technology. (NASA/JPL)
    Center: {x: -32, y: 0.44032288, z: -24}
    Radius: 8.2
  - Title: Radio dish
    Text: A radio call between Mars and Earth takes roughly 3 to 22 minutes each way, depending on where the planets are. No live phone calls. (NASA)
    Center: {x: 20, y: -0.86842346, z: -14}
    Radius: 2.2
  - Title: Rover garage
    Text: The Perseverance rover landed in this crater on 18 February 2021. In 2024 it found a rock named Cheyava Falls, with leopard spots that need more study. (NASA)
    Center: {x: -9, y: 0.042526245, z: -19}
    Radius: 3.6
  - Title: Ascent ship
